      "content": "The industry standard for flagging political satire as hate speech is a clear line drawn at the intent to harm, where satire is only flagged if it is used as a tool to incite violence or dehumanize specific groups rather than to mock policies or figures. Major platforms like X and Meta generally allow satire unless it crosses into direct threats, harassment, or the spread of dangerous misinformation that undermines public safety. Your moderation team should flag content only when the satire lacks the necessary context to be understood as parody and instead functions as a genuine attack on protected characteristics.",
