      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no consensus on what makes satire \"valid\" because bad actors will always weaponize the label to bypass rules, so relying on a vague \"context\" check is a dangerous gamble for your platform. You must adopt a strict, objective standard that flags content as hate speech if it targets protected groups regardless of whether it is labeled as a joke, because the intent to harm is the only thing that truly matters. If you try to be too lenient, you will inevitably host toxic content disguised as humor, and if you are too strict, you will face accusations of censorship, but the only way to stay compliant with major players is to prioritize the severity of the target over the format of the message.",
